    "lang": "java",
    "pr_title": "Add support for HAProxyMessageEncoder",
    "pr_body": "Motivation:\r\n\r\nAdd support for HAProxyMessageEncoder.\r\nThis should help java based HAProxy server implementations propagate proxy information.\r\n\r\nModification:\r\n\r\nAdd public constructors for `HAProxyMessage`, `HAProxyTLV`, `HAProxySSLTLV`.\r\nAdd additional argument checks for `HAProxyMessage` and modify exceptions thrown when creating via public constructors directly.\r\nIntroduce a `@Sharable` `HAProxyMessageEncoder` which encodes a `HAProxyMessage` into a byte array.\r\nAdd an example `HAProxyServer` and `HAProxyClient` to `io.netty.example`\r\n\r\n\r\nResult:\r\n\r\nFixes #10164 \r\n",
    "pr_comments": [
        "Can one of the admins verify this patch?",
        "@jrhee17 please sign our icla and let me know once done:\r\n\r\nhttps://netty.io/s/icla ",
        "Done \ud83d\udc4d ",
        "cc: @argha-c",
        "One thing that keeps bugging me is the `HAProxySSLTLV` implementation.\r\n\r\n1. When decoded via `HAProxyMessageDecoder`, the `ByteBufHolder.content()` contains the entire raw content. (`client`, `verify`, `tlvs`)\r\n2. When instantiating, the content isn't set.\r\nhttps://github.com/netty/netty/blob/2699088dbba8bd30bb907056f70feaec0f064b31/codec-haproxy/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/haproxy/HAProxySSLTLV.java#L45\r\n\r\nTechnically, I don't think `HAProxySSLTLV` should be extending `ByteBufHolder` in the first place, but I am yet to find a clean solution.\r\n\r\nOtherwise, I feel pretty good about the rest of the pr.",
        "@jrhee17 maybe I am missing something but isn't the `HAProxySSLTLV`  thingy pre-existing ? If so I think we can't change it anyway atm... ",
        "> I think we can't change it anyway atm\r\n\r\nagreed..  I was trying to find a way to tackle this with minimal breaking changes but can't seem to find a clean solution.",
        "@netty-bot test this please ",
        "@carl-mastrangelo want to have a look as well ?",
        "@netty-bot test this please ",
